    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420">

                <pb facs="0500" n="396" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.00 Revolutions/253: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-15T11:00:00-03:00">July 15, 1932—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 15—10:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>65. My telegram of July 14, 2 p.m. I authorized the Consul General to approach
                    the Ministry of Marine with respect to the clearance of the steamers <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Delsud</hi> and the <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Angeles</hi>. Mr. Lee reports that
                    clearance was granted—<hi rendition="#italic">Angeles</hi> without, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Delsud</hi> with cargo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
